This document records capabilities proven on disk. NORTHSTAR defines the architecture. ROADMAP defines active sprint plans.

## 1. Ground Truth & Verification Proof

Verification requires source files under `ooda/` and passing execution of `./oodac/oodac check oodac/main.oo`.
Verification also requires C or LLVM emission followed by GCC or Clang compilation and execution.

## 2. Proven Capabilities

### Compiler Floor
- Pin: v0.221.1. WebAssembly Dual-Mode Compatibility & Browser Thread Isolation:
  The compiler supports automated dual-mode host engine fallback (`--target wasm-gc` / `wasm-linear` / `wasm-dual`).
  A sub-millisecond capability probe detects Wasm-GC support (< 0.01ms).
  HTTP isolation middleware (`std/net/http_isolation.oo`) and a ServiceWorker proxy (`coop-coep-shim.js`) enable `SharedArrayBuffer` on static hosts.
  The test suite passes 5/5 concurrency suites and 109/109 WebAssembly test suites with zero enforcer violations.

- Pin: v0.220.0. Sovereign WebAssembly (WASM) Backend 1.0 Finalized:
  The pure `.oo` binary generator operates without external toolchain dependencies.
  The generator implements LEB128 encoding, linear memory slab allocators, and WASI Preview 1 host calls (`fd_write`, `fd_read`, `proc_exit`).
  The optimizer provides peephole passes, tail-call optimizations (0x12), and dead-code elimination.
  The backend supports WASI Preview 2 WIT packaging, 128-bit SIMD (0xFD), shared memory atomics (0xFE), and DWARF 5 source maps.
  Verification passes in Wasmtime and Node.js V8 (109/109 E2E tests, 14/14 stress tests).

- Pin: v0.211.0. Live type check of `oodac/main.oo` passes OK across 179 modules.
- The primary product compilation path generates C code through `chs_rt` and compiles with GCC.
- `List[Name]` lowers to `OoL_Name` beside struct typedefs. `List[Float]` lowers to `OoFList` in `chs_rt`. Locks: `fixtures/list_struct_smoke.oo`, `fixtures/list_float_smoke.oo`. One-level nested lists lower to `OoLL_I`, `OoLL_S`, and `OoLL_F`. Locks: `list_ll_int_smoke.oo`, `list_ll_str_smoke.oo`, `list_ll_float_smoke.oo`.
- `Result` types emit as specialized structs (`OoResI`, `OoRes_Name`, `OoResLI`, `OoResB`, `OoResF`, `OoResLS`, `OoResLF`, `OoResV`). Locks: `result_int_smoke.oo`, `result_struct_smoke.oo`, `result_list_smoke.oo`, `result_bool_smoke.oo`, `result_float_smoke.oo`, `result_lstr_smoke.oo`, `result_lfloat_smoke.oo`, `result_void_smoke.oo`.
- `list_set` performs copy-on-write mutation. Out-of-range indices print `ERR` and terminate with exit code 1. Locks: `list_set_smoke.oo`, `list_set_oob.oo`.
- Mutable references `&mut Name` emit as C pointers with field write-through. Locks: `mut_struct_smoke.oo`, `deref_struct_smoke.oo`.
- User sum types compile to tagged structs. Pattern matching binds variant payloads. Missing sum arms fail type checking. Locks: `sum_shape_smoke.oo`, `sum_string_smoke.oo`, `sum_unit_smoke.oo`, `scripts/sum_exhaust_smoke.oo`.
- C code emission stamps `#line` directives before functions, control statements, and variable assignments. Locks: `scripts/c_line_smoke.oo`, `scripts/c_line_multi_smoke.oo`, `scripts/c_line_secret_smoke.oo`, `scripts/c_line_ctrl_smoke.oo`.
- Incremental compilation caching in `bootstrap/oodac_pure_build` caches emitted C files based on source SHA-256 digests.
- Product compilation flags use `-O2 -g -Werror=implicit-function-declaration -Werror=return-type -Werror=uninitialized`. Locks: `scripts/gcc_werror_impl_smoke.oo`, `scripts/gcc_werror_return_smoke.oo`.
- Diagnostic error reporting prints source paths, line numbers, column positions, and caret indicators (`^`). Locks: `scripts/diag_path_smoke.oo`, `scripts/diag_caret_smoke.oo`.
- Iteration over collections (`for x in xs`) lowers to length and index queries. Range loops (`for i in 0..n`) accept identifier bounds. Locks: `for_list_smoke.oo`, `for_ident_range_smoke.oo`.
- `Option[Int]` Some(0) and None compile to tagged `OoResI` structures. Locks: `option_int_smoke.oo`, `option_str_smoke.oo`.
