### Capability Model & Sandboxing
- Landlock Linux process isolation operates under `&SysCap` tokens (`oo_landlock_restrict`). Empty allowlists fail closed.
- POSIX resource limits (`setrlimit`) operate under `&SysCap` tokens for address space, open files, and CPU time.
- Process lifecycle management (`spawn`, `wait`, `kill`) sanitizes environment variables.
- Hostile capability probes verify that unauthorized environment access and forged tokens fail closed. Lock: `scripts/hostile_cap_probe_smoke.oo`.
- Process execution (`process_exec`) acts as a SECRET taint sink and requires explicit capability tokens.
- GPU kernel dispatch (`GpuCap`) provides CPU fallback execution and emits PTX text.
- HMAC token attenuation and process-local seals verify capability tokens in `chs_rt_caps.c`.
- Linear bump arenas operate under `&AllocCap` with O(1) allocation and bulk reset operations.

### Standard Library & Developer Tooling
- Product standard libraries reside in `ooda/std/` (org `std/src` is not product). Exactly 4,539 standard library modules are certified GREEN. Locks: `scripts/std_smoke.oo`, `scripts/std_product_honesty_smoke.oo`.
- Language Server Protocol (`ooda lsp`) provides hover, definition, and autocompletion over standard I/O. Lock: `scripts/lsp_complete_smoke.oo`.
- Package manager commands (`ooda add`, `ooda search`) verify Ed25519 signatures against registry indexes. Lock: `scripts/pm_store_search_smoke.oo`.
- Product CLI commands (`check`, `build`, `run`, `test`, `dump`, `outline`, `reflect`, `fix`, `patch`) operate natively in `cli/main.oo`.
- Cryptographic primitives provide SHA-256 hashing, HMAC-SHA256, and AES-128-ECB block encryption.
- Test runner (`ooda test`) executes verification blocks and assertions under `OODA_TEST=1`.
- Automated repair tool (`ooda fix`) patches common compiler errors under `OODA_FS_WRITEDIR` permissions. Lock: `scripts/emust_autofix_smoke.oo`.
- Master quality assurance harness (`qa/qa_master.oo`) executes 22 test suites with zero failures.
- Multi-backend emission produces bit-identical output across consecutive runs. Lock: `scripts/bit_identical_emit_lock.oo`.

